<title>RUSSIA: Russian 238-day T-bill yields 29.71 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 238-day T-bill yields 29.71 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 238-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 29.71 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had expected the yield to be between 28.15 and 29.58 percent.</p>
<p>The 22068 bills maturing on November 8, 1997, the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed on Tuesday at 87.62 to yield 23.66 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number	     22075</p>
<p>    Issue volume		7.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	    8.46 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	    6.86 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		    5.75 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	     83.77 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price   83.41 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     29.71 pct</p>
<p>Highest accepted yield  30.50 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 238 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     October 29, 1997</p>
<p>On March 5, the Finance Ministry will offer 4.50 trillion roubles ($790 million) in an additional tranche of 133-day T-bills (series 22069) and repay about 8.60 trillion roubles in maturing 210-day T-bills (series 22044).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($ = 5696 Russian Roubles)</p>
